Describe commands as JSON (for agents and scripts)

Without arguments, lists every command in one JSON object. With a command path, describes that
command: arguments, flags, output fields and examples. Always prints JSON, whatever --output says.
Does not use the network.

Usage:
  mdr schema [<command>...] [flags]

Arguments:
  <command>   command path, e.g. "project get"

Flags:
      --all   describe every command, one JSON object per line

Global flags (-o, --fields, --full, --dry-run, ...): see mdr --help

Examples:
  mdr schema
  mdr schema schema
  mdr schema --all
